  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A mixture of hydrogen and oxygen has volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2000</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, pressure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mi>kPa</mi></math> and mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>76</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>. The ratio of number of moles of hydrogen to number of moles of oxygen in the mixture will be</p><p>[Take gas constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p>",
    "image": null
